/*
 * Tideline — German source strings (task #129).
 *
 * Convention: SOURCE STRING IS THE KEY. SwiftUI's `Text("...")` accepts a
 * `LocalizedStringKey` and looks up the literal here. So a call like
 *   Text("Willkommen bei Tideline.")
 * looks up `"Willkommen bei Tideline." = "..."` in this file. The
 * value side of the entry is just the literal German again (or a
 * tweaked variant); the EN equivalent lives in `en.lproj/Localizable.strings`.
 *
 * When the German source copy changes, BOTH this entry and its EN
 * twin must update in the same commit.
 *
 * Sections roughly mirror the view file the string lives in.
 */

